WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.963
Step four plans wave zero.

2
00:00:01.963 --> 00:00:04.697
The playbook says wave zero is ready:

3
00:00:04.697 --> 00:00:08.162
one server to connect,
none blocked in the CMDB.

4
00:00:08.162 --> 00:00:12.331
Show the newest wave zero plan,
and it has one row: web oh one,

5
00:00:12.331 --> 00:00:16.588
in the portal dev resource group,
in West US 2, in AzureCloud,

6
00:00:16.588 --> 00:00:21.112
state ready, with the exact tag
string the connect would write.

7
00:00:21.112 --> 00:00:26.522
Look at the tags: the configuration item,
Config Owner set to machine configuration,

8
00:00:26.522 --> 00:00:29.502
the environment, the
location, the owning team,

9
00:00:29.502 --> 00:00:32.951
the patch group, and Patch
Owner set to Update Manager.

10
00:00:32.951 --> 00:00:37.075
That's the plan a reviewer reads
and files before anything runs.

11
00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:40.175
Step five dry-runs the wave
with Microsoft's role.

12
00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:41.475
It exits zero.

13
00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:46.227
Web oh one reports that it would connect
to AzureCloud, in that resource group and

14
00:00:46.227 --> 00:00:51.050
region, authenticating with the managed
identity, and the connect task is skipped.

15
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.670
Web oh one doesn't exist, and
nothing tried to reach it.
